    "description": "2. Job Purpose To provide safe, effective, and patient-centered nursing assistance during dental examinations, treatments, and minor surgical procedures. The Dental Nurse supports dental professionals in delivering quality oral healthcare by preparing dental equipment, maintaining infection prevention and control standards, assisting patients, and ensuring the dental unit operates efficiently. 3. Key Duties and Responsibilities A. Patient Care and Assistance Welcome patients and provide appropriate assistance throughout dental visits. Prepare patients for dental examinations and procedures. Obtain and record vital signs when required. Provide pre- and post-procedure nursing care and instructions. Assist patients with special needs, anxiety, or discomfort. Maintain patient dignity, privacy, and confidentiality. B. Clinical and Procedural Assistance Assist dentists during dental examinations and procedures. Prepare and arrange dental instruments, materials, and equipment before procedures. Pass instruments and dental materials to the dentist during treatment. Assist during tooth extraction, scaling, fillings, root canal treatment, and other dental procedures within the authorized scope of practice. Prepare dental materials according to the dentist's instructions. Monitor patients during and after procedures and report abnormalities promptly. Assist in emergency management within the scope of nursing competence. C. Infection Prevention and Control Clean, disinfect, and sterilize dental instruments according to hospital IPC protocols. Ensure proper use of personal protective equipment (PPE). Maintain cleanliness of dental chairs, work surfaces, and treatment areas. Segregate and dispose of medical and sharps waste appropriately. Follow standard precautions and infection prevention guidelines. Monitor sterilization processes and maintain relevant records. D. Equipment and Supply Management Check the functionality and readiness of dental equipment. Monitor dental supplies, consumables, and instruments. Maintain adequate stock and report shortages to the concerned supervisor. Ensure proper storage and handling of dental materials. Report damaged or malfunctioning equipment promptly. E. Documentation and Reporting Maintain accurate patient nursing records and procedure-related documentation. Document sterilization and infection prevention activities. Record used materials and consumables as required. Report incidents, complications, and patient safety concerns. Maintain confidentiality of patient information. F. Professionalism and Quality Improvement Follow hospital policies, procedures, and professional ethics. Participate in departmental meetings, training, and quality improvement activities. Support patient satisfaction and service quality initiatives. Work collaboratively with dentists and other healthcare professionals. Perform other related duties assigned by the immediate supervisor within professional competence.",
