    "description": "To provide professional, efficient, and confidential secretarial and administrative support to the General Manager by managing appointments, meetings, correspondence, records, communication, and follow-up activities. The position ensures effective coordination between executive management, departments, employees, and external stakeholders, enabling the executive to perform managerial responsibilities efficiently and ensuring that assigned tasks and decisions are followed up on time. 1. JOB DESCRIPTION 1.1. Main Duties and Responsibilities A. Executive Schedule and Appointment Management Manage and maintain the executive's daily, weekly, and monthly schedule. Arrange appointments, meetings, conferences, and official engagements. Coordinate meeting dates and times with relevant departments and participants. Prioritize appointments based on urgency, importance, and executive instructions. Remind the executive of upcoming meetings, appointments, and important deadlines. Adjust schedules when changes occur and communicate updates to concerned parties. B. Meeting Coordination and Documentation Prepare meeting agendas in consultation with the executive and concerned departments. Organize meeting venues, required documents, equipment, and participant lists. Attend meetings as assigned and accurately record minutes. Prepare and distribute meeting minutes to authorized participants. Record decisions, action points, responsible persons, and deadlines. Follow up on meeting decisions and report pending actions to the executive. Maintain organized records of meetings and executive decisions. C. Correspondence and Communication Management Receive, screen, and manage incoming letters, emails, telephone calls, and other communications. Prepare, type, edit, and proofread official letters, memoranda, reports, and other documents. Forward correspondence to the appropriate departments or individuals based on executive instructions. Ensure timely preparation and dispatch of outgoing correspondence. Maintain a correspondence register and track important documents. Communicate professionally with employees, management, visitors, customers, and external stakeholders. Ensure that official communications are accurate, properly formatted, and submitted on time. D. Executive Administrative Support Provide daily administrative support to the executive. Prepare briefing materials, presentations, reports, and reference documents. Collect information from departments as requested by the executive. Organize documents required for executive decision-making. Assist in preparing official travel arrangements, including transportation, accommodation, and itineraries. Receive visitors and arrange appointments with the executive. Coordinate the executive's official activities with relevant departments. Perform other administrative duties assigned by the immediate supervisor. E. Document and Records Management Maintain an organized filing system for executive correspondence, reports, meeting minutes, and decisions. Register, classify, and file incoming and outgoing documents. Maintain both electronic and physical records in accordance with company procedures. Retrieve documents promptly when requested by authorized personnel. Ensure the accuracy, completeness, and proper handling of executive records. Protect confidential documents from unauthorized access. Ensure proper document retention and transfer in accordance with company policy. F. Follow-up and Coordination Follow up on tasks and instructions assigned by the executive to departments and responsible employees. Maintain a follow-up register showing assigned activities, responsible persons, deadlines, and progress. Request progress updates from concerned departments. Identify overdue assignments and bring them to the attention of the executive. Coordinate communication between the executive and departmental heads. Prepare periodic follow-up reports on pending and completed assignments. Ensure that executive instructions are communicated accurately and implemented within the required timeframe. G. Confidentiality and Professional Ethics Maintain strict confidentiality of executive communications, company information, and official documents. Handle sensitive information professionally and responsibly. Avoid unauthorized disclosure of company information. Maintain professional conduct, integrity, and impartiality. Ensure that confidential documents are securely stored and accessed only by authorized personnel. Comply with company policies, procedures, and applicable laws. H. Office Management and Other Duties Ensure the availability of necessary office supplies and secretarial materials. Maintain the proper functioning of office equipment and report technical problems. Keep the executive's office documents and working materials organized. Coordinate with relevant administrative units to facilitate executive activities. Support the preparation of official events, conferences, and management meetings. Perform other related duties assigned by the immediate supervisor.",
